Welcome to the war table. A {% term id="module" %}module{% /term %} is one page in the sidebar of GGE Command. Each module edits one or more {% term id="plugin" %}plugins{% /term %}, the jobs your bot does. Pick a module, pick the account at the top, change its settings and save.

{% terms_on_page /%}

{% screenshot id="sidebar" alt="The sidebar of GGE Command with the Attacks and gear group open. Each module is one page, and a Soon tag marks a module that is not built yet." /%}

A module with several plugins shows them as tabs, as a panel for each {% term id="kingdom" %}kingdom{% /term %}, or one below the other. Each plugin keeps its own switch on the {% ui key="client:module.status" /%} card or in its panel.

## Overview {% #overview %}

- [Live view](/modules/live-view/) shows what the bot last read from the game: castle stores, marches and session gains.

## Account manager {% #account-manager %}

- [Wheel spin](/modules/wheel-spin/) spins the event wheels with the tickets you hold, keeps a reserve and stops at your daily limit.
- [Messages](/modules/messages/) copies your alliance chat to a Discord channel and sends what you write there back to the game.

## Attacks and gear {% #attacks-and-gear %}

- [Towers](/modules/towers/) attacks {% term id="robber-baron" %}Robber Baron{% /term %} towers in all four kingdoms, each kingdom with its own switch.
- [Fortress](/modules/fortress/) attacks the {% term id="fortress" %}fortresses{% /term %} in Burning Sands, Everwinter Glacier and Fire Peaks.
- [Nomads, Samurai and Daimyo](/modules/nom-sam-daimyo/) attacks {% term id="nomad" %}Nomad{% /term %} and {% term id="samurai" %}Samurai{% /term %} camps during their events.
- [Storms](/modules/storms/) attacks the {% term id="storm-islands" %}Storm Islands{% /term %} fortresses and sends {% term id="mead" %}mead{% /term %} to your Storm Islands castle.
- [Khan](/modules/khan/) attacks {% term id="khan-camp" %}Khan camps{% /term %} during the Khan event, {% term id="taunt" %}taunts{% /term %} the Khan and can refill your defence.
- [Green Berimond](/modules/green-berimond/) attacks the camps of the {% term id="berimond-invasion" %}Berimond Invasion{% /term %} event with event {% term id="tool" %}tools{% /term %}.
- [{% ui key="client:modules.berimond.name" /%}](/modules/berimond/) attacks the watchtowers of the {% term id="berimond" %}Berimond{% /term %} kingdom from your camp during the Berimond Kingdom event, and keeps the camp stocked with troops.
- [Invasion events](/modules/invasion-events/) attacks {% term id="foreign-lord" %}Foreign Lords{% /term %} and {% term id="bloodcrow" %}Bloodcrow{% /term %} camps for {% term id="glory" %}glory{% /term %}.
- [Blade Coast](/modules/blade-coast/) plays the Blade Coast event, from building the camp to attacking the Kraken, and never pays with {% term id="ruby" %}rubies{% /term %}.
- [Virtual presets](/modules/virtual-presets/) saves attack {% term id="wave" %}waves{% /term %} under a name, so any attack module can send them.
- [Armourer](/modules/armourer/) buys siege tools with coins when a castle runs low.

## Utilities {% #utilities %}

- [Recruit, tools and heal](/modules/recruit-tools-heal/) keeps each castle's troops and tools at the stock you set.
- [Refinery and Toolsmith](/modules/refinery-toolsmith/) builds siege and defence tools in your workshops up to the stock you set, and keeps your Refinery and Toolsmith crafting the components you pick.
- [Auto-feast](/modules/auto-feast/) starts feasts in castles that hold more food than they need.
- [Equip sell](/modules/equip-sell/) sells the equipment colours you pick and loose gems from storage, never set pieces.
- [Daily chores](/modules/daily-chores/) claims the login bonus, sends the tax collector out and asks your alliance for help.
- [Troop transfer](/modules/troop-transfer/) sends troops and tools from one kingdom to another when a kingdom runs low.
- [Alliance donations](/modules/alliance-donations/) gives your alliance the resources and coins your castles can spare, and gives to the Colossus during its event.
- [Native village](/modules/native-village/) spends olive oil, charcoal and glass on the native village pack you pick.

## PvP {% #pvp %}

- [Alert and autostation](/modules/alert-autostation/) moves a castle's troops to a protected alliance castle before a player's attack lands.

## Discord {% #discord %}

- [Discord attack alerts](/modules/discord-attacks/) posts attacks on you, and your own attacks, to Discord channels.
- [Discord event alerts](/modules/discord-events/) keeps one Discord message up to date each for the fortresses, the {% term id="aquamarine" %}Aquamarine{% /term %} Islands and the Aquamarine Towers.

## Account settings are not a module {% #account-settings %}

The pause between attacks, the {% term id="daily-attack-limit" %}daily attack limit{% /term %}, the {% term id="time-skip" %}time skips{% /term %} the bot may spend and the {% term id="shutoff-timer" %}shutoff timer{% /term %} belong to the account, not to a module. Edit them on the {% ui key="client:drawer.accountSettings" /%} tab of the account. See [Open an account](/war-room/dashboard/#account-drawer).

## The attack cap {% #attack-cap %}

Your {% term id="attack-cap" %}attack cap{% /term %} is the most attack plugins one account can have on at once. It is 4, 6 or no limit. GGE Command sets it for your user, and it applies to each of your accounts on its own. If no one changed it, it is 4.

The cap counts plugins, not modules. Several modules share it because many modules hold more than one attack plugin:

- Towers has one attack plugin for each kingdom, so up to 4.
- Fortress has one for each kingdom, so up to 3.
- Nomads, Samurai and {% term id="daimyo" %}Daimyo{% /term %} has 2, and Invasion events has 2.
- Storms, Khan and {% ui key="client:modules.green-berimond.name" /%} have 1 each. The **Mead replace** tab of Storms does not count.
- Armourer, Blade Coast, {% ui key="client:modules.berimond.name" /%}, {% term id="virtual-preset" %}Virtual presets{% /term %} and the modules outside Attacks and gear do not count.

So with a cap of 4, all four Towers kingdoms leave room for nothing else. The {% ui key="client:module.status" /%} card of each attack module shows how many attack plugins are on and your cap. When you reach the cap, the other switches lock and show {% ui key="client:plugins.attackLimitReached" /%}.

If you save more attack plugins than the cap allows, the save fails. If an account already has too many on, its bot does not start.

## Ideas every attack page shares {% #shared %}

### Source castle {% #source-castle %}

The {% term id="source-castle" %}source castle{% /term %} is the castle an attack leaves from. On Towers, Fortress, Khan, {% ui key="client:modules.green-berimond.name" /%} and Nomads, Samurai and Daimyo, you pick it in **Castle to attack from**. The list holds the castles you have in that kingdom: the {% term id="main-castle" %}main castle{% /term %}, {% term id="outpost" %}outposts{% /term %}, a capital, and in the {% term id="great-empire" %}Great Empire{% /term %} a metropolis. Left empty, the bot uses the main castle there. If the castle you picked is gone, the bot falls back to the main castle and the status tells you.

Other modules leave from a fixed castle. Storms uses your Storm Islands castle, and Invasion events use your main castle in the Great Empire.

### Commanders {% #commanders %}

Every attack module has one {% ui key="client:plugins.commanderPicker.title" /%} card. It holds one list for every attack on the page.

- Choose the tiles in the order the bot should send each {% term id="commander-game" %}commander{% /term %}. Choose a picked tile again to take it out.
- No tile is picked until you pick one. With none picked, the bot sends any of your commanders, in the order that suits each attack.
- {% ui key="client:plugins.commanderPicker.all" /%} picks every commander, and {% ui key="client:plugins.commanderPicker.clear" /%} picks none.
- Dimmed numbers are commanders you don't have yet. The bot skips them until you do.
- The bot uses each commander for one attack at a time. While a commander marches, the next free one in your list goes.

The picker also has a {% term id="vip" %}VIP{% /term %} tile and a {% ui key="client:plugins.commanderPicker.vipCap" /%}, the most VIP commanders the bot may use each day. It never goes beyond the free daily allowance of your VIP level. The bot saves the cap now but does not use VIP commanders yet. {% status kind="planned" /%}

### Army: Autofill or Waves {% #army %}

Every attack module has an **Army** setting with two choices.

- {% ui key="client:army.mode.autofill" /%} lets the bot fill each attack from the castle's troops and tools. The settings below it, such as sides, waves, tools and **Unit order**, steer how it fills.
- {% ui key="client:army.mode.waves" /%} sends exactly the waves you write. Write them on the page, or pick a [virtual preset](/modules/virtual-presets/) to reuse the same waves on several pages.

A plan in Waves is never swapped for {% term id="autofill" %}Autofill{% /term %} behind your back. If the waves can't be sent as written, the module stops and the status says why.

### Tools {% #tools %}

Most attack modules put siege tools in the first wave, and event tools in later waves during events. Some modules can also buy tools from the armourer for their own castle when it runs low. The [Armourer](/modules/armourer/) module does the same for any castle you list.

### Log only {% #log-only %}

Khan, Storms, {% ui key="client:modules.green-berimond.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.berimond.name" /%}, Invasion events and Nomads, Samurai and Daimyo have a {% term id="log-only" %}**Log only**{% /term %} setting. With it on, the bot builds each attack and writes it to the {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %}, but sends nothing to the game. Towers and Fortress don't have it. See [Test with Log only first](/playing-it-safe/#log-only).

### Distances in clicks {% #clicks %}

GGE Command measures map distances in {% term id="click" %}clicks{% /term %}, one square of the map. **Search radius** on Towers is how far from the source castle the bot looks for targets. With **Horse** set to **By distance**, targets farther than **Feather beyond** get a {% term id="horse-feather" %}fast horse feather{% /term %} and nearer ones get the {% term id="coin-horse" %}coin horse{% /term %}.

### Daily caps and other limits {% #limits %}

- The account's **Daily attack limit** counts the attacks of every attack module. It is 3,500 by default and at most 4,000, the game's own limit for 24 hours.
- Every attack module of an account shares a limit of 600 attacks an hour.
- Towers has **Most attacks a day** and **Attacks an hour** for each kingdom.
- Nomads and Samurai have **Attacks per run** and **Time skips a day**.
- Khan, Nomads, Samurai and Invasion events can stop at a score you set.

## Modules still to come {% #soon %}

Modules marked Soon in the app have no page here yet. They are: {% ui key="client:modules.castle-manager.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.offer-buyer.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.overseers.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.food-manager.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.rift-raid.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.leveller.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.blacksmith-event-shops.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.coin-farmer.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.bth-blacksmith.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.influence-farming.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.recruiter.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.castle-builder.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.equipment-manager.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.or-storms.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.mp-builder.name" /%} and {% ui key="client:modules.asset-monitor.name" /%}.

Each one has a page in the app that says what it will do. Choose {% ui key="client:module.soon.contact" /%} on that page to open the [Contact](/contact/) page and tell us you want it.

{% screenshot id="coming-soon" alt="The Castle manager page, a module marked Soon: a Coming soon tag, one line on what the module will do, and the Ask for it button." /%}

## Related errors {% #errors %}

- [PLUGIN_ATTACK_CAP](/errors/#plugin-attack-cap): the settings do not save because too many attack plugins are on.
- [TOO_MANY_ATTACK_PLUGINS](/errors/#too-many-attack-plugins): an account has more attack plugins on than the cap allows, so its bot does not start.
- [PLUGIN_OPTION_ARMY](/errors/#plugin-option-army): an army setting can't be read.
